    "description": "From the ai-teammate review round on #226 (lib/src/js/job_runner.dart:137).\n\nAfter a successful `action` return, a `drainTimers()` failure propagates and fails the whole run on the MAIN engine, but the WORKER path swallows it (`catch (_) {}`, rationale: a drain failure must not mask the job's own result/error). Same situation, two policies, currently undocumented.\n\nOptions: (a) swallow-with-a-log on the main engine too; (b) document why the main engine deliberately surfaces drain failures (nodeCompat scripts whose timer chains ARE the job's side effects must not silently lose callbacks). No Java spec exists (GraalJS has no timers) — this is a Dart-side contract decision; pick one and pin it with a test."
  }
